This script blocks requests to known tracking domains using the `chrome.webRequest` API.

```javascript
// Hardcoded list of tracking domains (can be expanded or loaded dynamically)
const TRACKING_DOMAINS = [
  "tracking.com",
  "ads.example.com",
  "pixeltracker.net",
  "analytics.co"
];

chrome.webRequest.onBeforeRequest.addListener(
  (details) => {
    const url = new URL(details.url);
    const isTrackingDomain = TRACKING_DOMAINS.some(domain => {
      const regex = new RegExp(`\\.${domain}$|^[^\.]+\.${domain}$`);
      return regex.test(url.hostname);
    });

    if (isTrackingDomain) {
      console.log(`Blocked tracking request: ${url.href}`);
      return { cancel: true };
    }
  },
  { urls: ["<all_urls>"] },
  ["blocking"]
);
```

